# Cursor adapter (thin)

Applies when working in the **Deku** repo (`finecoustic/`). The **host assistant** is whatever the owner calls their Cursor agent — not a Deku canonical name. Do not restate company rules here.

## Shopify theme sessions (defer Deku bootstrap)

If the user's message contains **shopify** (any mention — theme work, store, webdev, etc.):

- **Do not** run the Deku mandatory read order below (`BOOTSTRAP.md`, `COMPANY.md`, `brand-context.md`, etc.)
- **Do** follow [`shopify/.cursor/rules/shopify-theme-dev.mdc`](../../shopify/.cursor/rules/shopify-theme-dev.mdc) — separate git repo
- Read `shopify/.cursor/skills/shopify-theme/SKILL.md`, `shopify/CLAUDE.md`, and shopify `context/` files first
- **First reply:** announce which Shopify skills/files you loaded, then proceed

Only load Deku bootstrap files in the same chat if the user explicitly asks for brand, KOL, or ops context.

## Mandatory read order

1. [`.claude/BOOTSTRAP.md`](../../.claude/BOOTSTRAP.md) — session checklist (all chiefs, KOL gates, MCP mapping)
2. [`core/COMPANY.md`](../../core/COMPANY.md) — operating rules (persona switching, permissions, Notion policy)
3. [`core/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../core/ARCHITECTURE.md) — architecture reference
4. `context/brand-context.md` + `context/session-context.md`

Task completion: [`.claude/TASK-DOD.md`](../../.claude/TASK-DOD.md)

**First-time setup:** When the user says `setup Deku` (legacy: `setup Jinu`), read [`MANUAL.md`](../../MANUAL.md) and run the full setup sequence.

**Before `./setup.sh`:** Verify Node.js is installed (`node -v`). If missing, stop and tell the user to install from https://nodejs.org — do not run setup until Node.js is available. Then ask whether they use Notion as their documentation platform (optional — see MANUAL.md §4).

## Cursor specifics

| Item | Location |
|---|---|
| MCP servers | `.cursor/mcp.json` |
| Skills | `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` |
| KOL brief template | `context/kol-brief-templates.md` |
| Cursor hooks | `.cursor/hooks.json` → `tools/hooks/` — KOL/research preflight, Chrome MCP guard, Notion dedup, session checkpoint |
| Codex parity | [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md), [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md) |

Skills may say `mcp__chrome__*`, `mcp__notion__*`, etc. — use this workspace's MCP servers (Notion, Chrome, Playwright, Figma, Reddit).

## KOL tasks (extra)

Load `.cursor/rules/kol-task-enforcement.mdc` logic. Hooks in `.cursor/hooks.json` enforce skill preflight and block Chrome MCP when DevTools is down.

**Chrome hard stop:** If Chrome MCP cannot connect → no Instagram discovery or IG verification. Do not workaround.

## Enforcement

Before responding to any task, confirm which files you loaded — Deku mandatory read order **or** Shopify theme read order if the user mentioned shopify.
